1
00:00:00,117 --> 00:00:01,892
This is AidBlink:

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:04,442
emergency aid in a single link,

3
00:00:04,692 --> 00:00:05,680
built on Solana.

4
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:09,763
Emergency aid breaks down in the last mile.

5
00:00:10,163 --> 00:00:12,300
Donors can't see whether their money became

6
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:12,975
real help.

7
00:00:13,375 --> 00:00:16,563
Organizations reconcile aid in spreadsheets.

8
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:18,975
The same benefit can be claimed twice.

9
00:00:19,375 --> 00:00:21,925
And the people receiving aid should never

10
00:00:21,925 --> 00:00:23,850
need a wallet or pay fees.

11
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:27,613
Our approach is to keep crypto exactly

12
00:00:27,626 --> 00:00:28,638
where it earns its keep:

13
00:00:29,075 --> 00:00:31,763
funding, transparency and auditability.

14
00:00:32,163 --> 00:00:34,613
And to keep the human flow simple

15
00:00:34,626 --> 00:00:35,476
and wallet-free.

16
00:00:36,646 --> 00:00:39,096
A supporter contributes through a Solana Blink.

17
00:00:39,496 --> 00:00:42,196
The organization allocates that pool to real,

18
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:43,709
pseudonymous needs.

19
00:00:44,121 --> 00:00:46,346
The person in need receives a one-time

20
00:00:46,346 --> 00:00:49,121
voucher, with no wallet and no fees,

21
00:00:49,396 --> 00:00:51,859
that a partner redeems exactly once.

22
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:53,720
Let me show it.

23
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:55,582
A supporter opens the Blink,

24
00:00:55,832 --> 00:00:59,270
connects Phantom, and sends a genuine Devnet transaction.

25
00:00:59,683 --> 00:01:00,745
This is not a mock-up:

26
00:01:01,183 --> 00:01:03,345
the contribution is confirmed on-chain.

27
00:01:04,542 --> 00:01:07,367
The organization dashboard reads the aid pool

28
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:08,929
live from the on-chain ledger:

29
00:01:09,467 --> 00:01:12,717
raised, available, allocated and redeemed.

30
00:01:13,104 --> 00:01:15,642
A budget guard prevents allocating more than

31
00:01:15,655 --> 00:01:16,667
was actually raised.

32
00:01:17,846 --> 00:01:20,696
Approving a request issues a signed voucher.

33
00:01:21,096 --> 00:01:22,596
The partner verifies it once;

34
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:25,108
a second attempt is rejected and logged.

35
00:01:25,508 --> 00:01:28,196
Single use is a server-side state transition,

36
00:01:28,596 --> 00:01:30,246
not a property of the QR code.

37
00:01:31,428 --> 00:01:32,916
We are explicit about the line.

38
00:01:33,328 --> 00:01:35,666
The Anchor program and the contributions are

39
00:01:35,666 --> 00:01:37,041
real, on Devnet.

40
00:01:37,441 --> 00:01:40,828
Benefit amounts, partners and redemption are simulated.

41
00:01:41,228 --> 00:01:43,366
Being honest about what's real is what

42
00:01:43,378 --> 00:01:44,903
makes the demo credible.

43
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:49,279
Solana Blinks make distribution unstoppable.

44
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,754
A contribution is just a shareable Action

45
00:01:51,754 --> 00:01:53,454
link, so any post,

46
00:01:53,679 --> 00:01:55,842
message or QR code can become a

47
00:01:55,854 --> 00:01:56,929
funding entry point,

48
00:01:57,217 --> 00:01:59,467
with any wallet and no app to install.

49
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:01,658
This is not a concept.

50
00:02:02,071 --> 00:02:03,996
We already have an Anchor program deployed

51
00:02:04,108 --> 00:02:05,558
and verified on Devnet,

52
00:02:06,008 --> 00:02:07,896
real donations tested end-to-end,

53
00:02:08,346 --> 00:02:10,221
and an open-source repo with a typed

54
00:02:10,221 --> 00:02:12,008
client and a public dashboard.

55
00:02:13,148 --> 00:02:16,436
Our go-to-market starts with community organizations and

56
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:20,398
NGOs in Brazil that already distribute emergency aid.

57
00:02:20,798 --> 00:02:23,336
Their existing channels become the distribution,

58
00:02:23,761 --> 00:02:25,623
and the model expands to any cause

59
00:02:25,623 --> 00:02:26,973
that pays out benefits.

60
00:02:28,147 --> 00:02:30,622
We are applying to Colosseum to pilot

61
00:02:30,634 --> 00:02:32,147
with real organizations,

62
00:02:32,522 --> 00:02:33,859
harden the on-chain program,

63
00:02:34,272 --> 00:02:36,384
and turn AidBlink into the standard way

64
00:02:36,509 --> 00:02:39,647
to fund aid transparently on Solana.
